WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:30.485
Emira Ivy has stayed alongside in Gossport UK with no recorded outings on the team's tracker for the past month. This is Offshore North Episode 10. Every four years, a handful of people set out alone to sail around the world without stopping or taking outside help, and one Canadian is working toward becoming the first to finish that race. On the Canadian boat, the team's YB tracker shows Emira Ivy alongside in Gossport UK as of October 19th, 2026, and it records no movement outside the birth in the preceding 30 days. On 8th October, the team posts

00:00:30.485 --> 00:00:35.645
that Scott Shire will not start the route to RUM. The post lays out an energy systems failure

00:00:35.645 --> 00:00:40.185
on the delivery back from Canada that limited the boat's function. A compressed qualification

00:00:40.185 --> 00:00:44.605
window once the systems were restored, and sea sickness that struck while Shire worked on the

00:00:44.605 --> 00:00:49.865
onboard computer in 25 knots upwind in the English channel. He turned back rather than continue

00:00:49.865 --> 00:00:54.965
in busy shipping lanes with incomplete alarms and navigation tools. The energy issue had already

00:00:54.965 --> 00:00:59.365
forced an earlier return to port during the transatlantic delivery, and the subsequent repair

00:00:59.365 --> 00:01:03.765
and computer upgrade work left too little margin to complete and test every safety system

00:01:03.765 --> 00:01:05.525
before the qualification deadline.

00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:10.685
Shire has spoken openly about his history with C-signus, and on this attempt, the symptoms

00:01:10.685 --> 00:01:15.085
arrive quickly while he was focused on the computer in a high traffic area where reliable

00:01:15.085 --> 00:01:18.185
radar, AI's, and collision avoidance overlays are essential.

00:01:18.625 --> 00:01:23.065
The decision to abort preserved the boat and the longer-term goal of a Vende Globe campaign

00:01:23.065 --> 00:01:26.645
rather than risking a compromise start to the 2026 season.

00:01:26.645 --> 00:01:32.025
That choice keeps the focus on the 2020-28 edition, where every completed grade 2 solo race

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:36.985
on Emira IV will count toward both the required qualifier and the Globe Series points table.

00:01:37.505 --> 00:01:42.285
A 14th October YouTube short from the team shows the boat under sail in mostly dry conditions.

00:01:42.805 --> 00:01:46.965
The short clip captures the boat moving in light air with the wing mast and foils visible,

00:01:47.385 --> 00:01:50.445
confirming that systems are operational again after the earlier faults.

00:01:51.025 --> 00:01:55.325
The video adds no new position data beyond the tracker, but demonstrates that the boat is

00:01:55.325 --> 00:01:58.045
ready for further work once the route do rum window closes.

00:01:58.605 --> 00:02:02.245
The choice to turn back in the channel lines up with the same kind of three in the morning

00:02:02.245 --> 00:02:05.325
risk call a pilot makes when systems and weather do not line up.

00:02:05.845 --> 00:02:06.605
Now the fleet.

00:02:07.639 --> 00:02:11.819
Ferrari unveiled its 100-foot foiling monohol this week at a yard near Pisa.

00:02:12.399 --> 00:02:17.399
The Verdea design is finished in yellow and matte dark gray, measures 30.5 meters long

00:02:17.399 --> 00:02:22.959
and up to 23.5 meters wide with foils deployed and is described as the world's first energy

00:02:22.959 --> 00:02:25.139
self-sufficient foiling offshore monohol.

00:02:25.139 --> 00:02:30.519
Construction took place inside two unremarkable sheds along the Navis-Heli Canal, with the team

00:02:30.519 --> 00:02:33.479
fitting out the space themselves after arriving four years earlier.

00:02:34.019 --> 00:02:37.759
The hull features the signature bustle, a central trimorand style structure running

00:02:37.759 --> 00:02:42.159
bow to stern that supports the rest of the hull, a concept Verdea previously applied

00:02:42.159 --> 00:02:47.839
to the AC-75 to recent IMAX such as DMG-Mori Global 1 and Group Dubroil.

00:02:48.279 --> 00:02:51.099
More than 20 CFD iterations refined the final shape.

00:02:51.099 --> 00:02:55.199
First, sailing trials are set for the end of the first quarter of 2027.

00:02:55.679 --> 00:02:59.599
The project required journalists to sign non-disclosure agreements and cover phone cameras

00:02:59.599 --> 00:03:03.959
before entry, underscoring the commercial sensitivity around a brand entering the offshore

00:03:03.959 --> 00:03:04.939
space at this scale.

00:03:05.439 --> 00:03:09.619
That launch shows how far the push for self-sufficient, high-performance offshore designs

00:03:09.619 --> 00:03:11.639
has moved beyond the current IMAQA fleet.

00:03:12.519 --> 00:03:17.199
The Vende Globe Foundation opened its 2027 call for projects on 16 October.

00:03:17.199 --> 00:03:22.359
associations and research bodies have until 31 October to apply for up to 50,000

00:03:22.359 --> 00:03:26.819
euros a year to support ocean knowledge, protection, or restoration work. The fund

00:03:26.819 --> 00:03:30.819
can support a project for up to three years and will not exceed 35% of total

00:03:30.819 --> 00:03:35.619
project cost, arriving only after other financing is secured. Past grants have

00:03:35.619 --> 00:03:39.479
funded citizen science algae surveys along the French coast with biolith and

00:03:39.479 --> 00:03:44.059
planet mayor, an algae-focused sailing expedition by Blutopia, an environmental

00:03:44.059 --> 00:03:47.159
DNA sampling in New Zealand waters by citizens of the sea.

00:03:47.639 --> 00:03:52.059
The call is open to non-profit structures in France and internationally, covering research,

00:03:52.319 --> 00:03:54.439
innovation, medical, and restoration topics.

00:03:54.879 --> 00:03:59.419
The fund ties the race's visibility directly to ongoing ocean research rather than one-off

00:03:59.419 --> 00:03:59.679
events.

00:04:00.299 --> 00:04:04.944
Time for plane sailing, and I'm a skipper at sea never gets a full night's sleep.

00:04:05.424 --> 00:04:08.964
The boat is moving at highway speeds through the dark, and the only way to keep it safe

00:04:08.964 --> 00:04:12.904
is to break rest into short fragments, usually around 20 minutes at a time.

00:04:12.904 --> 00:04:17.584
The autopilot handles most of the steering, but the skipper still has to wake, check the

00:04:17.584 --> 00:04:21.584
instruments, decide whether the route still makes sense, and then try to sleep again before

00:04:21.584 --> 00:04:26.264
the next decision point arrives. That pattern repeats for weeks. It is why every system

00:04:26.264 --> 00:04:31.264
on board, power, navigation, collision avoidance, has to work without constant human oversight,

00:04:31.624 --> 00:04:35.624
and why a single computer fault or power glitch can force a hard choice about whether to

00:04:35.624 --> 00:04:40.304
keep going. The 20-minute cycle is the real limit on how long one person can stay in command

00:04:40.304 --> 00:04:47.249
of a 60-foot boat alone. And the countdown. 755 days remain until the Vendée Globe start on

00:04:47.249 --> 00:04:53.029
November 12, 2028. The campaign's next concrete milestone is the Root-Durum start on November

00:04:53.029 --> 00:04:59.069
1, 2026, which Scott Shire will not contest. That's offshore north for this week. Every

00:04:59.069 --> 00:05:03.389
source is linked in the episode notes if you want to read further. If the show helps you follow

00:05:03.389 --> 00:05:08.689
the sport, a rating on Apple Podcasts or Spotify genuinely helps other people find it. I'm Dan,

00:05:08.689 --> 00:05:10.789
man, fair winds and eyes on the horizon.

